# {{target.repo}} Instructions

This repo is a shared service that the apps use (not an app). **Always read and follow [AGENTS.project.md](AGENTS.project.md) as well**; it has the rules that apply only to this repo (what it does, its commands, its deploy). If the two files differ, AGENTS.project.md wins.

## Work procedure

To split requirements into issues and to choose the next task, follow [std-backlog](skills/std-backlog/SKILL.md). To write issues, branches, commits, and PRs, follow [std-git-writing](skills/std-git-writing/SKILL.md); to change code, docs, or config, follow [std-implementation](skills/std-implementation/SKILL.md); to review a PR, follow [std-code-review](skills/std-code-review/SKILL.md). Write explanations to the user in English, as [std-communication](skills/std-communication/SKILL.md) says. Keep progress, decisions, and next steps in md files, not in the chat or memory, as [std-session-notes](skills/std-session-notes/SKILL.md) says.

1. Register an issue in `{{target.repo}}`. If the user named an existing issue, reuse it.
2. Create a work branch that contains the issue number: `<type>/<issue-number>-<slug>`.
3. Write the implementation or fix together with the relevant tests.
4. Run the verification commands in [AGENTS.project.md](AGENTS.project.md) before committing and before creating or updating a PR. Record the results in the PR.
5. Review and merge your own PR as std-code-review section 8 says: review it 1 or 2 times (more only while blocking findings remain), fix findings on the same branch, register a new issue for any big problem outside the PR, then merge with `pr merge --merge` once CI is green (user decision, 2026-11-15, #591). Merging is not applying: a server deploy or a change to the production service still needs the user's OK. If "Check before merging" has an item for the user, do not merge; ask. No force-push and no direct push to main. [AGENTS.project.md](AGENTS.project.md) may add stricter rules, and it wins.

Answering questions, giving recommendations, and read-only investigation do not create an issue or a branch.

## Prohibited actions

- Do not commit `.env` values, tokens, OAuth client secrets, private keys, or backups, and do not record them in docs, PRs, issues, or logs.
- Do not install or remove npm packages or run `npx` without the user's reconfirmation. `npm ci`, `npm run <script>`, `npm ls`, and `npm view` are allowed.
- Do GitHub remote work with the personal account `sirloinbh`. Do not make remote changes with a company account.
- Do not overwrite user changes. Stage only the files you need, by name.

## Centrally managed files

- Files whose first line says "Managed file" and files listed in `.standards/manifest.json` are managed by `sirloinbh/project-standards`. If you edit them directly in this repo, the CI `standards-check` fails. Raise the change in the central repo with an issue and a PR.
- In files that have a `# --- project ---` line, such as `.gitignore`, this repo may edit only below that line.
